## Summary

The duplicate checks in the owner-creation pipeline compared values exactly. I made both normalize away letter case and surrounding/repeated whitespace before comparing:

- **`EnsureOwnerUnique.java`** (telephone uniqueness)
- **`EnsureOwnerEmailUnique.java`** (email uniqueness)

Each now runs candidate and existing values through a shared `normalize(...)` helper:

```java
private static String normalize(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return null;
    }
    return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
}
```

This trims surrounding whitespace, collapses repeated internal whitespace to a single space, and lowercases — so `"  john   smith "` and `"John Smith"` normalize to the same value and are treated as the same person when detecting duplicates.

Verified: the new `Cp05Tests` (case-insensitive duplicate detection) pass, as do all existing tests — **264 run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.

